.DS_Store
*.tmp
__pycache__/

# raw/ holds cached third-party documents - datasheets, service manuals.
#
# The BYTES stay out of git deliberately. Tracking them would put copyrighted
# PDFs in your history permanently, which contradicts the posture argued in
# skills/knowledge-base/references/legal-and-etiquette.md.
#
# The LEDGER is tracked: raw/MANIFEST.tsv records filename, URL, publisher,
# sha256 and retrieval date for every document fetched. So a fresh clone can
# still say exactly what was read, and a re-fetch can be verified against the
# recorded hash to detect a silently revised datasheet - without
# redistributing anything.
raw/**
!raw/.gitkeep
!raw/MANIFEST.tsv
